{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/651984-my-first-vtr-2nd-ed-game","id":651984,"title":"My First VTR 2nd ed game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-04T19:37:13-07:00","id":651984,"title":"My First VTR 2nd ed game","content":"It starts tonight, after many months of reading, planning, converting and rebooting...<br /> <br /> In just a few minutes I will be running my first 2nd Ed game.<br /> <br /> It will mostly be a prelude set in the late 90s but I think I have this figured out. <br /> <br /> Wish me luck I'll post an After-Action Report sometime tommorow. Wish me luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T20:23:34-07:00","id":652051,"title":"","content":"Good luck!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T20:35:17-07:00","id":652057,"title":"","content":"I will not wish you luck, because I know you will do well.<br /> <br /> I will instead wish you lots of fun and a memorable chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T04:45:50-07:00","id":652274,"title":"","content":"Seconded. I's been a while since I've seen you around, is good to see known faces (masques, whatever) around again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T21:45:30-07:00","id":653489,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Had a busy sort of day so couldn't get back to this before now. (Also for some reason it wouldn't let me post this from my phone.)<br /> <br /> Firstly, thanks to ArcaneArts and Thorbes for having faith in my rusty ass (I haven't run a game in nearly 5 years.) And Charlaquin for the luck and for writing up the homebrew Galloi rules I'm using for this story. Those were extremely helpful and helped push me forward on this game as My Lady wanted to reboot her Galloi and I decided to remake my NYC setting.<br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The session (just a solo reboot Prelude of my lady's Gallio named Gehenna) went great. We tested out the new system in several ways, and here's what I found.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">* Is there no Prelude section in the book anymore? I searched for it but didn't find one. Not a huge deal but it through me off at the beginning.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">* I really, really, really love the changes to the Disciplines. Majesty, Dominate, and Nightmare especially.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">* The Social Maneuvering system works so well I want to cry. I wish the social roll system always needed this and I love the Doors and the Impressions.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">* The Beats are awesome and takes the ambiguity out of XP awards. Thank you Onyx Path for that.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">* The Humanity and Breaking Point system is also awesome. Nothing more to say but that is a natural growth to the old system and fit perfectly.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">* While introduced in the Mekhet clan book, I loved playing with the post humanous Embrace. Glad it's official rules now.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">So yeah. Great session with great new crunch. We didn't get through the whole Prelude. But we are playing again tonight.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Which leaves me with a question, would anyone be interested in a solo RP Actual Play about a Nosferatu Gallio in NYC? It would have converted characters from the CWOD (the Widows from MbN and the entire Cast of NYbN) as well as characters of my own design. <br /> <br /> If so I might just make a new topic about it.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T21:56:53-07:00","id":653500,"title":"","content":"Forgot one thing. Conditions are awesome and I'm going to make cards for them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T22:24:37-07:00","id":653513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/651984-my-first-vtr-2nd-ed-game?p=653489#post653489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Had a busy sort of day so couldn't get back to this before now. (Also for some reason it wouldn't let me post this from my phone.)<br /> <br /> Firstly, thanks to ArcaneArts and Thorbes for having faith in my rusty ass (I haven't run a game in nearly 5 years.) And Charlaquin for the luck and for writing up the homebrew Galloi rules I'm using for this story. Those were extremely helpful and helped push me forward on this game as My Lady wanted to reboot her Galloi and I decided to remake my NYC setting.<br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The session (just a solo reboot Prelude of my lady's Gallio named Gehenna) went great. We tested out the new system in several ways, and here's what I found.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">* Is there no Prelude section in the book anymore? I searched for it but didn't find one. Not a huge deal but it through me off at the beginning.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">* I really, really, really love the changes to the Disciplines. Majesty, Dominate, and Nightmare especially.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">* The Social Maneuvering system works so well I want to cry. I wish the social roll system always needed this and I love the Doors and the Impressions.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">* The Beats are awesome and takes the ambiguity out of XP awards. Thank you Onyx Path for that.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">* The Humanity and Breaking Point system is also awesome. Nothing more to say but that is a natural growth to the old system and fit perfectly.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">* While introduced in the Mekhet clan book, I loved playing with the post humanous Embrace. Glad it's official rules now.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">So yeah. Great session with great new crunch. We didn't get through the whole Prelude. But we are playing again tonight.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Which leaves me with a question, would anyone be interested in a solo RP Actual Play about a Nosferatu Gallio in NYC? It would have converted characters from the CWOD (the Widows from MbN and the entire Cast of NYbN) as well as characters of my own design. <br /> <br /> If so I might just make a new topic about it.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>That's awesome, I'm glad you're enjoying it, and that my Galloi writeup worked well for you. I would love to see the AP, especially since I never had an opportunity to playtest that Galloi homebrew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T04:00:02-07:00","id":653694,"title":"","content":"Ha! Glad to know you found all the changes in the sytem to your taste. Yeah, 2nd edition Requiem is a huge improvement on all fronts, at least in my personal and humble opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T12:17:56-07:00","id":654228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/651984-my-first-vtr-2nd-ed-game?p=653500#post653500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgot one thing. Conditions are awesome and I'm going to make cards for them</div> </div> </div> </div>You can find condition cards on drivethrurpg in PDF and POD if you want to save time : <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/124846/Vampire-The-Requiem-2nd-Edition-Condition-Cards\" target=\"_blank\">http://drivethrurpg.com/product/1248...ondition-Cards</a> and <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/122721/GodMachine-Condition-Cards\" target=\"_blank\">http://drivethrurpg.com/product/1227...ondition-Cards</a><br /> <br /> Always glad to read AP!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/824-araknee","name":"Araknee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}